    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #332\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed successfully to `bb/relay-126-mcp-integration-05-07-project-granted-thr_t6vd2txmt5`.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplements issue #126: adapts active MCP tool registrations into a project's agent-tool availability, extending `generatePermissionManifest`'s permission facts with MCP as a fourth source.\n\n- Added `getGrantedMcpAgentTools` (`backend/packages/data/src/mcp/mcpAgentTools.ts`): joins active `mcpServers` items, active `mcp_tool_registrations`, and `project_mcp_grants.granted = true` for a given project, returning each tool's synchronized schema/description snapshot along with its `requiresApproval`/`riskClass`.\n- Wired this into `PermissionManifest` as a new `agentTools` field (`backend/packages/data/src/manifest/permissionManifest.ts`), computed fresh on every call — deactivating a server/registration or revoking a grant removes a tool immediately, without touching its audit history.\n- Exported the new type/function from `@semprec/data`'s public surface (the user-only grant mutations remain intentionally unexported, per #124's grant-write restriction).\n- Added integration tests covering: granted tool inclusion with correct approval metadata, exclusion when ungranted/inactive-registration/inactive-server, and two projects exposing different subsets of the same server — plus an end-to-end case through `generatePermissionManifest`.\n\nVerified: full monorepo build, dependency-boundary check, and the full unit/integration/e2e test suites all pass (build clean; boundaries clean; 83 unit + 572 integration + 5 e2e tests passing, including the new MCP tests).\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
